      <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h2</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"section-title"</span>&gt;</span>The Origin &amp; Revelation of ImanI[cite: 1]<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h2</span>&gt;</span>
      <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"doctrine-card"</span>&gt;</span>
        <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">style</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-main);"</span>&gt;</span>
          Moving away from assigned, descriptive adjectives like "black" that describe a shadow or condition, <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">strong</span>&gt;</span>ImanI<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">strong</span>&gt;</span> is a proper noun representing a sovereign ontology, a spiritual nationality, and a return to original character[cite: 1].
        <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span>
        <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"grid-3col"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">style</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"margin-top: 8px;"</span>&gt;</span>
          <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-card"</span>&gt;</span>
            <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">span</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-num"</span>&gt;</span>Origin[cite: 1]<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">span</span>&gt;</span>
            <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h4</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-title"</span>&gt;</span>Faith in Action[cite: 1]<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h4</span>&gt;</span>
            <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-desc"</span>&gt;</span>Rooted in the Swahili concept of <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">em</span>&gt;</span>Imani<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">em</span>&gt;</span> (Faith), transforming passive belief into active alignment with divine law and collective purpose[cite: 1].<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span>
          <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span>
          <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-card"</span>&gt;</span>
            <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">span</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-num"</span>&gt;</span>Grammar of Spirit[cite: 1]<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">span</span>&gt;</span>
            <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h4</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-title"</span>&gt;</span>Proper Noun Identity[cite: 1]<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h4</span>&gt;</span>
            <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"pillar-desc"</span>&gt;</span>Replacing modifiers that depend on external systems with a sovereign name that declares self-existence and heritage[cite: 1].<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span>
