"></div></div></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1708603972="" class="presented-response-container ng-tns-c1708603972-261" jslog="283401;track:impression,attention" data-hveid="2"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1708603972="" class="response-container-content ng-tns-c1708603972-261"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2984337282="" highlighttoaskhost="" class="response-content ng-tns-c1708603972-261"><!----><thinking-overlay _ngcontent-ng-c2984337282="" _nghost-ng-c3439656023="" class="enable-luminous-fast-follows ng-star-inserted"><!----></thinking-overlay><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2984337282="" class="model-response-label-announcer" aria-live="off" aria-busy="false"><!----><!----><h2 _ngcontent-ng-c2984337282="" class="cdk-visually-hidden screen-reader-model-response-label ng-star-inserted"> Gemini said </h2><!----><!----></div><!----><structured-content-container _ngcontent-ng-c2984337282="" class="model-response-text processing-state-visible ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c912621556="" style="height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c912621556="" class="container"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c912621556="" _nghost-ng-c3228108065="" id="message-content-id-r_804cf7f228faf357" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3228108065="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel md-content enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color stronger tutor-markdown-rendering" id="model-response-message-contentr_804cf7f228faf357" aria-busy="false" aria-live="off" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p data-path-to-node="0">The names in the previous code (like "The Sovereign Genesis" or "Agreement 01") were example placeholders I created to show how the 3 category tabs would look. Because web browsers run in a secure sandbox, <b data-path-to-node="0" data-index-in-node="206">a webpage cannot look inside your hard drive and read your actual file names on its own</b>.</p><p data-path-to-node="1">To fix this so you don't have to write code, here is an updated version of the <b data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="79">Audio Vault</b> that gives you a direct <b data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="115">"📁 Load Your Audio Files"</b> button right on the page.</p><h3 data-path-to-node="2">What This Update Does:</h3><ul data-path-to-node="3"><li><p data-path-to-node="3,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">One-Click Folder Loader:</b> You click <b data-path-to-node="3,0,0" data-index-in-node="35">"📁 Load Audio Folder"</b> or <b data-path-to-node="3,0,0" data-index-in-node="61">"➕ Add Audio Files"</b>, select your songs directly from your computer, and the website will automatically read their real titles, organize them, and build your clickable playlist on the spot.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="3,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Category Auto-Sorting:</b> When you select files from your <code data-path-to-node="3,1,0" data-index-in-node="55">ImanI story</code>, <code data-path-to-node="3,1,0" data-index-in-node="68">The mysteries</code>, or <code data-path-to-node="3,1,0" data-index-in-node="86">Audio Agreements</code> folders, it automatically sorts them into their matching category tabs.</p></li></ul><p data-path-to-node="4">Here is your updated <code data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="21">index.html</code>:</p><response-element class="no-md" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><code-block _nghost-ng-c362045847="" class="ng-tns-c362045847-267 enable-luminous-code-block ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c362045847="" class="code-block ng-tns-c362045847-267 ng-animate-disabled ng-trigger ng-trigger-codeBlockRevealAnimation" jslog="223238;track:impression,attention;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_804cf7f228faf357&quot;,&quot;c_054f4193c616e860&quot;,null,&quot;rc_db21c0